{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "3D Handles",
  "summary": "Turn a button on the item into a 3D handle: an arrow each way it moves, a ring for a turn, and a drag along it.",
  "order": 9,
  "practice": "../_scenes/arm_on_item.blend",
  "steps": [
    {
      "title": "Step 1: Reach as a Handle",
      "text": [
        "1. In the Kneady tab's tree, click Reach.",
        "2. Click 3D Handle.",
        "3. Hover the forearm: Reach is an arrow on the forearm now, pointing the way its Up / Down moves the hand.",
        "",
        "The arm is as Buttons on the Item left it. A 3D handle keeps its direction in the scene as you orbit, and a drag goes along it. It points along what it drives: a Move's axis, or the way a Rotate turns."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "01_handle.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].handle",
          "is": "HANDLE"
        },
        {
          "hovered": "Forearm",
          "object": "Arm"
        }
      ],
      "start": {
        "mode": "OBJECT",
        "select": [
          "Arm"
        ],
        "active": "Arm",
        "sidebar": "Kneady",
        "view": {
          "location": [
            0.102,
            0.031,
            -0.02
          ],
          "rotation": [
            0.71238,
            0.44106,
            0.28736,
            0.46412
          ],
          "distance": 0.8,
          "perspective": "PERSP"
        },
        "set": [
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_on",
            "value": true
          },
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_labels",
            "value": "ALWAYS"
          },
          {
            "path": "scene.kneady_highlight",
            "value": "OUTLINE"
          },
          {
            "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].tree_open",
            "value": true
          },
          {
            "path": "window_manager.kneady_row",
            "value": -1
          },
          {
            "path": "window_manager.kneady_pick",
            "value": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 2: An Arrow Each Way",
      "text": [
        "1. Set Reach's Shape to Quad Arrow.",
        "2. Set its Size to 2.",
        "3. Hover the forearm: two double arrows cross at Reach's place, one for each way it moves the hand.",
        "",
        "Up / Down runs along one arm and Left / Right along the other; an arm seen end on dims, and takes no drag. A Ring suits a turn; a Box, a scale. Size is this handle's own, against Handle Size at the top of the tab."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "02_quad.mp4",
          "label": "In the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].handle_shape",
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].handle_size"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].handle_shape",
          "is": "CROSS"
        },
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[1].handle_size",
          "at_least": 1.9
        },
        {
          "hovered": "Forearm",
          "object": "Arm"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 3: Drag Along It",
      "text": [
        "1. Hover the forearm, then drag one of Reach's arrows along itself: the hand goes the way it points, and follows the mouse.",
        "",
        "Drags Prefer Single Direction, on for Reach, keeps the drag to the arm you go along most."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "03_haul.mp4",
          "label": "On the forearm",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "operator": "kneady.drag",
          "with": {
            "target": "Arm",
            "region": 1,
            "button": 1
          },
          "moved": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 4: Bend on a Ring",
      "text": [
        "1. Click FK on the forearm: the arm is in FK, and Bend shows in place of Reach.",
        "2. In the tree, click Bend, click 3D Handle, and set its Shape to Ring.",
        "",
        "A ring lies about the axis its Rotate turns on - here the elbow's."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "04_ring.mp4",
          "label": "On the forearm, then in the Kneady tab",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "highlight": [
        "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].handle_shape"
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].handle",
          "is": "HANDLE"
        },
        {
          "path": "objects[\"Arm\"].kneady.regions[0].buttons[0].handle_shape",
          "is": "RING"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Step 5: Turn It",
      "text": [
        "1. Hover the forearm, then drag around Bend's ring: the forearm bends as far as you sweep.",
        "",
        "Seen face on, a ring turns by the angle you sweep around its middle; seen edge on, by how far you drag along its rim, as you would turn a wheel."
      ],
      "media": [
        {
          "file": "05_turn.mp4",
          "label": "On the forearm",
          "paragraph": 0,
          "recorded": {
            "blender": "5.2",
            "kneady": "1.0.0"
          }
        }
      ],
      "done_when": [
        {
          "operator": "kneady.drag",
          "with": {
            "target": "Arm",
            "region": 1,
            "button": 0
          },
          "moved": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
